/-! # S2: square tail, SYNTACTIC variant (no frame needed): pool 724 hosted on a compare carry

`entryR L0 k = pmapR (merged …) = pmapR (comparePart …) ++ pmapR (s2RTail …)`.  The comparison
carries `cR = base 256 … 511` are erased by measurement in `compareChain` (each carry's last
write is its own `eraseCarry`) and never used by the tail (`s2RTail_tight`: tail ⊆ `tSites`).
So the tail can host pool 724 (the carry `w 722`) on `h300 = pmapR L0 (base 300)`:
`entryRHs k = hostRename entryPairs (cpR k) ++ swap(hole724, h300) (hostRename entryPairs (tlR k))`.
