In the re-planned staircase the first checkpoint (letter 425, budget 87) is
packed at the end of the division forward pass and unpacked at the start of
the multiplication reverse pass.  Both run inside
`Rolling1588Lifetime.phaseHost`, where the record walk keeps its b-rail on the
x I/O word.  The pieces below move the b-rail onto `bSite`, relabel the codec
by `phaseRelabel` so that it acts on the same physical sites as in the field,
and move the b-rail back for the record unwalk.

`phasePieces_good`: every wire of these pieces has, through the phase
placement, an image in the record arena that avoids all 59 omissions.
