section Merge_StairInventory_at_StairSideA

/-!
Static inventory and numeric ledger for the eight-checkpoint staircase.

The qubit lemmas deliberately accept the final placed omission list as an
argument.  The codec/segment/loan adapters must prove that their concrete 68
(or fallback 65) sites satisfy this interface; no unproved placement is baked
into the inventory theorem.
-/

section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxRecDepth 30000
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.unnecessarySeqFocus false

namespace ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairInventory

open ECDSAAdd Arithmetic Challenge
open MappedCompressed






/-! ## Concrete 68-site omission support

The proposed physical omission list differs from the logical retired-role
list only at its first three sites.  Making that relationship explicit avoids
an unchecked list-level placement assertion in the final inventory proof.
-/














/-! Exact count ledger from PK2 section 7.4. -/












/-! Conservative gate-slot ledger.

The codec entries are exact static slot totals from the generated gate dumps.
Orientations cost three slots per Fredkin.  A generic loan is bounded by an
eight-slot complemented majority plus a six-slot complemented erasure, i.e.
fourteen slots.  `StairLoan.loanWindow_slots_le` proves this local bound.
-/

def bestCodecSlotsPerKernel : Nat := 8108 + 6407 + 5075 + 3656 + 2725 + 1757 + 1173 + 582
def bestSlotDelta : Nat := 2 * (bestCodecSlotsPerKernel + 3 * 486 + 14 * 20620) + 14 * 68

theorem bestSlotDelta_eq : bestSlotDelta = 640194 := by decide +kernel

theorem best_program_slots (old new : Program)
    (oldBound : gateSlots old ≤ 50515743)
    (delta : gateSlots new ≤ gateSlots old + bestSlotDelta) :
    gateSlots new ≤ 51155937 := by
  rw [bestSlotDelta_eq] at delta
